// golden_set.jsonl — shared golden set for Parts A, B, and C.
//
// Format: one JSON object per line. Lines starting with // are ignored by
// the runner (each part's main() strips them before parsing). Built once
// here — the same 15 questions run against all three parts, which is what
// makes the eval deltas between parts mean something instead of being
// noise from different test data.
//
// Schema (per row):
//   {
//     "query": "the user's question",
//     "expected_citations": ["...zero or more expected doc filenames..."],
//     "expects_revision": true | false   // true if this question is hard
//                                        // enough that Part A's Critic
//                                        // (no correction) is expected to
//                                        // NOT approve it on the first pass
//   }
//
// Grounded against the real Day 2 knowledge base documents
// (labs/day2/python/data/docs/) — reuse the SAME Foundry IQ knowledge
// base, nothing new to provision.
